# Root build-context excludes (MDRS-16).
#
# All six app images build with `context: .` and `file: ./apps/<app>/Dockerfile`,
# so BuildKit reads THIS file (or `<dockerfile>.dockerignore`) and nothing else.
# The old per-app .dockerignore files were never consulted and have been deleted.
#
# Rule of thumb: exclude only things the image rebuilds for itself. Every
# workspace manifest, every lib source tree and every `.env.example` must stay
# in the context — the Nx build inside the image depends on them.

# Version control. `.git` is a file, not a directory, in a git worktree, so it
# is useless inside the image either way.
.git
.gitignore
.git-blame-ignore-revs
.github
.husky

# Anything the image installs or compiles itself.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/dist
**/.turbo
**/.nx
**/.tsbuild
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/coverage
**/test-results
**/storybook-static
**/.keycloakify

# Local environment files. The build stage seeds `.env` from `.env.example`,
# which must therefore survive the exclusion below.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Editor / OS / tooling noise. `.claude/` can hold git-ignored WORKTREES of
# this very repository (`.claude/worktrees/<name>/`); with it in the context,
# Nx sees every project twice and `nx build` refuses with "set a unique name
# for each project" — measured on a local `docker build` during MDRS-86. CI
# runners never have the directory, which is why only local builds broke.
.claude
.vscode
.idea
.mcp.json
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log
**/*.swp

# Docker inputs themselves — BuildKit reads the Dockerfile out of band.
**/Dockerfile
**/.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
docker/

# Docs and migration scratch. Nothing in the build graph reads these.
**/*.md
docs/
.migration/
local_docs/
# The committed mirror of the claude.ai/design project (see
# .claude/skills/medaris-design-system/SKILL.md). Reference material for
# people and agents; no app imports it.
design-system/
